<title>finland: Valmet 1996 profit rises 66 percent.</title>
<headline>Valmet 1996 profit rises 66 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31-</p>
<p>					   (million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after financial items		 1,056 vs 637</p>
<p> Earnings per share (markka)		  10.26 vs 6.74</p>
<p> Net sales					 11,764 vs 8,574</p>
<p> Operating profit				   921 vs 530</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' median forecast for Finnish paper machine maker Valmet Oy had been for a 1,010 million markka profit after financial items.</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (markka)		    3.00 vs 1.75</p>
<p> Gross profit				    2,778 vs 2,107</p>
<p> Marketing and sales expenses		  733 vs 579</p>
<p> R&amp;D expenses					404 vs 306</p>
<p> Administrative expenses			 720 vs 692</p>
<p> Net financial items			gain 115 vs 27 gain</p>
<p> Share in profits of associated companies   20 vs 80</p>
<p> Extraordinary income			     82 vs 113</p>
<p> Extraordinary expenses			  118 vs 31</p>
<p> Profit before minorities, taxes	   1,020 vs 719</p>
<p> Taxes						 200 vs 54</p>
<p> Minorities				  charge 14 vs 9 charge</p>
<p> Net profit					  806 vs 656</p>
<p>  Equity to assets ratio (percent)	  42.8 vs 40.6</p>
<p>    NOTE - Full name of Finnish paper machine maker is Valmet Oy.</p>
<p>    -- Helsinki newsroom +358 9 6805 0235</p>
